{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
I [G]heard, I heard the old man say,
John Ka[D]naka-naka, tu-lai-[G]e!
To[G]day, today is a holiday,
John Ka[D]naka-naka, tu-lai-[G]e!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Tu-[G]lai-e, oh, tu-lai-e!
John Ka[D]naka-naka, tu-lai-[G]e!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
We'll [G]work tomorrow, but no work today,
John Ka[D]naka-naka, tu-lai-[G]e!
We'll [G]work tomorrow, but no work today,
John Ka[D]naka-naka, tu-lai-[G]e!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
We're [G]bound away for 'Frisco Bay,
John Ka[D]naka-naka, tu-lai-[G]e!
We're [G]bound away at the break of day,
John Ka[D]naka-naka, tu-lai-[G]e!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: G}
